 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9 }`, custom metric ids included) and adds a top-level `passed` flag plus a `thresholds` list of `{ metric, min, score, passed }`; invalid thresholds throw a `ThresholdError`. `frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min>` uses this to exit 1 on failure.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
